{
  "statement": "The Safety & Reliability of the bookkeeping system is paramount. SAF-01 ensures accurate recording of transactions, crucial to prevent data loss. SAF-02 mandates double-entry bookkeeping, enhancing integrity. SAF-03 guarantees an audit trail for accountability, vital for regulatory compliance. SAF-04's error handling is essential for fault tolerance, while SAF-05 ensures users can access critical functionalities during outages. SAF-06 validates currency conversions to prevent discrepancies, and SAF-07 emphasizes regular backups to safeguard data. These requirements collectively establish a robust safety framework essential for user trust and operational continuity.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["TRU-03", "SAF-03"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "TRU-03's requirement for a 5-year audit trail conflicts with SAF-03's 7-year retention, creating a logical inconsistency in audit trail duration."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-06", "SAF-06"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "SAF-06's validation of currency conversions may compete with EFF-06's requirement for real-time completion of currency conversion operations."
    }
  ],
